      "writtenOn": "2026-03-19T23:01:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need to define `GERRIT_VERSION` here?\nWe were used to having it in `version.bzl` and loading it.\n\nI am concerned that every time we make a new release we would need a new Library-Compliance +1, which doesn\u0027t make sense.",
      "parentUuid": "187f5742_8fb9eb6f",
      "revId": "bf3e0a8d27fd99a3d97c0f77b3139b475faca002",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57ba5800_c5930d47",
        "filename": "MODULE.bazel",
        "patchSetId": 45
      },
      "lineNbr": 4,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T21:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question.\n\nBazel modules don’t support load() in MODULE.bazel, and since plugin packaging is now delegated to bazlets, the API version needs to be exposed as a repository rather than a loaded symbol.\n\nTo keep the release process simple and avoid requiring LC+1 for routine updates, I moved both:\n\n* the GERRIT_VERSION, and\n* the bazlets dependency (pin)\n\ninto a dedicated MODULE fragment (`bazlets.MODULE.bazel`), which is then included from the root module.\n\nThis way, changes like version bumps or bazlets updates don’t require modifying MODULE.bazel itself, avoiding unnecessary churn in the main module file.\n\nI also aligned the version to 3.13.5-SNAPSHOT to avoid any skew between Bazel (authoritative) and the POMs.\n\nHappy to adjust if you’d prefer a different structure.",
      "parentUuid": "0eeedf7c_3016869f",
      "revId": "bf3e0a8d27fd99a3d97c0f77b3139b475faca002",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    }
